  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A simple pendulum and a mass–spring system oscillate with the same time period. The mass of the pendulum bob and the mass on the spring are initially identical. The masses are halved.</p>\n<p>What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{time period of pendulum}}{\\textit{time period of mass-spring system}}\"></span> when the masses have been changed?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
